 &nbsp;

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:39.480
For more than 120 kilometers, the Tren Maya will&nbsp;
even pass through the Calakmul Biosphere Reserve,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:43.500
one of the largest protected natural areas in&nbsp;
all of Mexico and one of the most important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:48.120
Mayan archaeological sites. A place that is&nbsp;
considered a World Heritage Site by UNESCO.

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:52.740
The indigenous population does not seem to&nbsp;
be enthusiastic either. Among other reasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:56.460
perhaps because more than 2,000&nbsp;
families have been displaced.
 &nbsp;

00:14:56.460 --> 00:15:01.320
("This project is not planned for us,&nbsp;
the common people [...] It is a tourism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:05.880
project that will only benefit the rich and&nbsp;
foreigners. We, who are the owners of the land,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:09.720
will only see it go by, because there&nbsp;
are no planned resorts for the majority&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:14.820
of our communities" – Open Letter from the&nbsp;
Indigenous Communities of the Yucatan in 2018)
 &nbsp;

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:19.680
Well, VisualPolitik viewers, these are the three&nbsp;
great positives and the three great negatives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:23.760
of one of the largest infrastructure&nbsp;
projects of recent decades in Mexico.
 &nbsp;

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:33.480
In any case, if one thing seems clear, it is not&nbsp;
only that the Tren Maya is clearly here to stay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:37.860
but also that it has the opportunity to be a&nbsp;
turning point for one of the poorest regions of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:42.480
Mexico. Of course, we have already seen that there&nbsp;
are some drawbacks. Mitigating those problems will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:47.220
have to be the goal of the Mexican government&nbsp;
over the next few years. Only time will tell.

